cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Semantic Afterlife: Long-Run Dynamics of Large Language Models Beyond the
  Context Horizon
message: >-
  If you use this software or its artifacts, please cite it. Once the manuscript
  is released, cite the paper instead and this repository as the software.
type: software
authors:
  - name: llm-semantic-afterlife contributors
repository-code: https://github.com/AdamCage/llm-semantic-afterlife
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-30"
keywords:
  - large language models
  - dynamical systems
  - Markov state models
  - semantic drift
  - context window
  - metastability
  - non-equilibrium dynamics
abstract: >-
  A reproducible experimental framework for studying long-run generation under
  an imposed finite sliding window. After the seed is evicted, the closed
  Stage 0–7 record supports a textual repetition lock on one instruct
  generator and between-seed last-band distinguishability of ten fixed seed
  texts (not recovered prompt memory). Metastable macrostates (H1) are not
  established. The software logs every run with a manifest.
